===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pro-|*h₂eyḱ-}}
From {{der|en|enm|fraught}}, {{m|enm|fraght}}, {{m|enm|freght|t=transport of goods or people (usually by water); charge for such transport; facilities for such transport; cargo or passengers of a ship; ballast of a ship; goods in general; (''figurative'') burden; charge}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|pos=n|id=MED17589}}</ref> from {{der|en|dum|vracht}}, {{m|dum|vrecht}}, or {{der|en|gml|vracht}}, {{m|gml|vrecht|t=cargo, freight; charge for transport of goods}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*fra-aihtiz}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*fra-|pos={{glossary|intensifying}} {{glossary|prefix}}}} + {{der|en|gem-pro|*aihtiz|t=acquisition; possessions, property}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂eyḱ-|t=to come into possession of, obtain; to own, possess}}).<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=8263947680|date=December 2023}}</ref> {{doublet|en|freight}}.

